---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Routes from "../../components/Routes.astro";
import Rule from "../../components/Rule.astro";
import { textChoices } from "../../lib/source.ts";

const M = "server/src/iki_server/entities/models.py";
const S = "server/src/iki_server/entities/services.py";
const kinds = textChoices(M, "RevisionKind");

const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: "Every change is a numbered revision" },
  { id: "how", label: "What a revision keeps, and how history is read" },
  { id: "rules", label: "The rules in full" },
  { id: "ref", label: "Routes, files and decisions" },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title="Every change is a numbered revision">
    <p>
      Each change to a record writes a <code>Revision</code>, numbered from 1, saying what kind of
      change it was, which fields it set, who made it, how, through which agent, and why; and a full
      row of the record's values into the history table of each table it touched. Both are
      append-only. The record's current revision number is the API's ETag: a client must send back
      the one it read to change it. A field's provenance is the latest revision that set it (<Adr
        n="0035"
      />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title="What a revision keeps, and how history is read">
    <p>
      <Path p={S} sym="def _revise(" /> inserts the <code>Revision</code> and bumps <code
        >Entity.revision</code
      > in the change's transaction; <Path p={S} sym="def _write_history(" /> then writes the history
      rows at that number. A revision keeps:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>kind</code> and <code>changed_fields</code>, from the table below;</li>
      <li><code>user</code>, <code>via</code> (web, API, MCP, command line, system, or <code>run</code> for a run's results), <code>client</code> (the OAuth app) and <code>agent</code>;</li>
      <li><code>reason</code>, when one was given or needed;</li>
      <li>for a state change, the field and the states from and to, and the signatures that set it, in order;</li>
      <li>for a record's first revision, the identity as submitted, where it was spelled other than its entry's.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>The ETag.</strong> <code>GET /api/v1/entities/{"{ref}"}</code> sends the revision as{" "}
      <code>ETag</code>. A change sends it back as <code>If-Match</code>: without one it's refused
      (428), and a stale one is refused (412) rather than overwriting someone else's change. <code
        >If-Match: *</code
      > is refused too, since it would skip the check. Setting a state names the revision the same
      way.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Reading the past.</strong> A record at revision <em>n</em> is, for each of its tables,
      the latest history row at or before <em>n</em>. <code>GET …/revisions/{"{number}"}</code>{" "}
      answers with it. A field's provenance is the latest revision that set it (<Path
        p={S}
        sym="def provenance("
      />); a record of a registry entry reads its entry's values' provenance from the entry's
      revisions. The record's audit trail, the Audit trail tab and its CSV, is its revisions, and its
      entry's (<Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/trails.py" />).
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Label</th><th>Note in the code</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {kinds.map((k) => <tr><td><code>{k.value}</code></td><td>{k.label}</td><td>{k.note}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>The kinds, read from <Path p={M} sym="class RevisionKind" />.</p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title="The rules in full">
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="What can never change" open>
        <p>
          <code>iki_revision</code> and every <code>__history</code> table are append-only twice over:
          a trigger refuses UPDATE, DELETE and TRUNCATE for every role, the owner included, and the
          app's role has no UPDATE or DELETE on them (<Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/operations.py" sym="class AppendOnly" />,{" "}
          <Path p="server/src/iki_server/entities/migrations/0002_history_append_only.py" />). The
          roles and grants are on <PageLink to="Audit trail" hash="roles" />.
        </p>
        <p>
          Only a plugin's migration changes kept history, and only to rename a field or a type or to
          convert a quantity to a new unit. Each records what it did in <code>iki_history_change</code>,
          signed by the deployment's key, so a signature made before reads its record through it (<Adr
            n={[33, 148]}
          />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/models.py" sym="class HistoryChange(" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="An agent's changes name the person and the agent" id="agents">
        <p>
          A change an agent makes names both: <code>Revision.agent</code> and <code
            >AuditEvent.agent</code
          > point to an append-only <code>Agent</code> row, stored once per distinct agent, with
          the OAuth client's ID and name, the person's grant, the MCP session, and the software and
          model it reported. The model comes from the <code>Iki-Agent-Model</code> header, which Iki
          can't check, and is shown as reported (<Adr n="0072" />, <Path
            p="server/src/iki_server/audit/models.py"
            sym="class Agent("
          />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/security.py" sym='MODEL_HEADER = "Iki-Agent-Model"' />).
          Guards read the agent too, as <code>actor.agent</code> and in each state change's history.
          What a delegated token may do, and why each lab role must belong to both the service
          account and the person, is on <PageLink to="Tokens and delegation" />.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Archive, detach and purge">
        <p>
          Records are archived, not deleted: <code>set_archived</code> writes an <code>archived</code>{" "}
          or <code>restored</code> revision, and is refused for registry entries and locked records
          (<Adr n="0008" />, <Path p={S} sym="def set_archived(" />). A detached plugin's records are
          kept and frozen: its tables are read-only to the app (<Adr n="0091" />). Purging a detached
          plugin's data leaves the core row of each record as a tombstone, with the SHA-256 of its last
          values, which proves what existed without keeping it (<Adr n="0092" />, <Path
            p={M}
            sym="class Tombstone("
          />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/purge.py" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Where the ADRs and the code differ">
        <ul>
          <li><Adr n="0007" /> names a <code>PropertyProvenance</code> table; <Adr n="0035" /> dropped it: provenance comes from revisions.</li>
        </ul>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title="Routes, files and decisions">
    <Routes paths={/^\/api\/v1\/entities\/\{ref\}\/(revisions|provenance|contributors)[^]*$/} />
    <div class="refs">
      <div>
        <h3>Where</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><Path p={M} sym="class Revision(" /></li>
          <li><Path p={S} sym="def _revise(" /></li>
          <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/api/trails.py" />: a record's trail and its CSV</li>
          <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/audit/log.py" sym="def current_agent(" /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Decisions</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><Adr n="0008" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0035" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0072" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0092" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0148" title /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
